From: Sangbaek Park <sangbaekpark@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 09:36:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [M159] media: Retain decoder ownership in DecoderSelector
 until delivery runs

Original change's description:
> media: Retain decoder ownership in DecoderSelector until delivery runs
>
> DecoderSelector::RunSelectDecoderCB() previously moved the selected
> Decoder and DecryptingDemuxerStream directly into a task posted to
> `task_runner_`. Until that task ran, neither DecoderSelector nor
> DecoderStream owned them.
>
> If pipeline teardown (e.g., WebMediaPlayerImpl::Shutdown() posting
> PipelineImpl::RendererWrapper::Stop() and DestructionHelper) ran ahead
> of that queued task on the media thread, destroying DecoderStream and
> DecoderSelector did not destroy the selected Decoder or
> DecryptingDemuxerStream. DestructionHelper could then destroy the
> CdmContext / AesDecryptor (and its CallbackRegistry) on the main thread
> before the media thread dropped the cancelled task, causing a
> use-after-free in ~DecryptingDemuxerStream() and
> CallbackRegistry::Unregister().
>
> Keep `decoder_` and `decrypting_demuxer_stream_` owned by
> DecoderSelector until a weak-bound DeliverSelectedDecoder() task runs
> and hands ownership synchronously to `select_decoder_cb_`. If
> DecoderSelector is destroyed before delivery runs, ~DecoderSelector()
> now invalidates pending tasks and synchronously destroys `decoder_` and
> `decrypting_demuxer_stream_` before returning, aborting selection with
> kFailed.
>
> Verified with new unit tests and by running the browser ASan repro on
> gLinux before (reproduces the UAF in CallbackRegistry::Unregister) and
> after the fix (no crash/ASan error).
>
